== Controls
- #strong[C2, hyperelliptic, `q = 3`, exhaustive] (`ctrlH-q3-run-20261024T2151Z`). The trace histogram is identical to round 3’s, with no odd `t`.
- #strong[C3, non-hyperelliptic, `q = 3`, exhaustive.] This reproduces round 3’s 9 prime-order classes exactly: split `t = 11`, non-split `t = −1`, and cone `t = −7` (×3), `t = 9` (×3, one with `|Aut| = 3`) and `t = −1`. The mass is `8 + 1/3`.
- #strong[C4, Theorem 5 negative control.] Hyperelliptic Res-shaped curves have no odd `t` (this control concerns hyperelliptic curves only):
  - `q = 5`: 119,496 Res-shaped among 38,397,517 squarefree forms (`ctrlH-q5-run-20261024T2156Z`);
  - `q = 7`: 55,040 among 41,985,520 (`ctrlH-q7-run-20261024T2158Z`).
- #strong[C5.] Res-shaped curves whose trace has no elliptic curve are excluded: 66,096 of 630,927 at `q = 3`, and 24,353 of 347,784 at `q = 5`. Matching L-polynomials is necessary, not sufficient.

